WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.630
Long ago, one finch-like bird
reached the islands of Hawaii.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.340
Its descendants, the
Hawaiian honeycreepers,

3
00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:10.620
became dozens of species,
with beaks for nectar,

4
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.610
seeds, insects and grubs.

5
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:20.170
One way a new species starts: a river, a
sea or mountains split a population apart.

6
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.220
But can a new species appear
right beside its parents,

7
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.710
or even in a single generation?

8
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.160
In this mission, you'll put two
routes to a new species side by side:

9
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.600
allopatric and sympatric.

10
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.630
Then you'll pin down the one thing both
routes need before the gene pools can

11
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.900
split apart.

12
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:42.560
Your mission: find out whether a new
species can appear beside its parents,

13
00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.730
and how fast.
